From 72f94c55d25e9d7b04d7aa82eb99981ac2e5f192 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fmillion <47171880+fmillion@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:15:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 43/45] platform/x86: lenovo: add ThinkPad X1 Fold Gen 1
 keyboard dock driver

The X1 Fold Gen 1 describes its magnetic keyboard dock as ACPI device
LEN009E (\_SB.DEVD): GDST() reports whether the keyboard rests on the lower
half of the folding panel, GDSZ() the panel area it covers, and the firmware
notifies the device (0x01) on changes. The state comes from the ECLite
firmware on the ISH, so it is only fresh once intel_ishtp_eclite is bound
(probe defers until \_SB.ECLT.ECLA is set).

Expose it through sysfs on the platform device: keyboard_docked (pollable,
KOBJ_CHANGE on change) and occlusion ("x y width height"). Userspace uses
it to switch between the full panel and the docked 1536x1006 mode. After
resume the lid state is resynchronised (\_SB.LID0.UNLS) and the dock state
re-read.

Previously developed out of tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
